\alias{CalibratorOneVsRest}
\title{One-vs-rest calibrator}
\description{
Applies a binary \link{Calibrator} separately to each class and returns class scores that are
row-normalized by the base \link{Calibrator} lifecycle.

For two classes, the wrapper fits exactly one wrapped calibrator on the original probability
matrix and preserves the package convention that column 1 is the modeled positive event.
For more than two classes, it fits one independent calibrator per class against a collision-safe
rest label and extracts the calibrated score of the original class.

Simple normalization follows Zadrozny and Elkan (2002).
Normalized one-vs-rest outputs are not guaranteed to be fully multiclass-calibrated
(Kull M, Perello Nieto M, Kängsepp M, Silva Filho T, Song H, Flach P (2019).
\dQuote{Beyond Temperature Scaling: Obtaining Well-Calibrated Multi-Class Probabilities with Dirichlet Calibration.}
In \emph{Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems}, volume 32, 12295-12305.
\url{https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2019/hash/8ca01ea920679a0fe3728441494041b9-Abstract.html}.; Arad A, Rosset S (2025).
\dQuote{Improving Multi-Class Calibration through Normalization-Aware Isotonic Techniques.}
In \emph{Proceedings of the 42nd International Conference on Machine Learning}, volume 267, 1574-1603.
\url{https://proceedings.mlr.press/v267/arad25a.html}.).

Direct \link{CalibratorPlatt} is binary-only; multiclass Platt uses \code{clb("ovr")} (Platt by default).
Other binary calibrators such as isotonic or beta may be supplied.
}
\references{
